<section>
    <h2>Contract work</h2>

    <p>
        I take on a small amount of contract
        <a href="/windows-app-development">Windows app development</a> alongside my role at Muse
        Group. Desktop apps in C# and XAML (<abbr title="Windows App SDK">WinUI</abbr>,
        <abbr title="Windows Presentation Foundation">WPF</abbr>,
        <abbr title="Universal Windows Platform">UWP</abbr> and Avalonia), native C++ work,
        migrations, and packaging and distribution.
    </p>

    <p>If you&rsquo;re emailing about a project, it helps to know:</p>

    <ul>
        <li><p>What the app is, and roughly who uses it.</p></li>
        <li><p>What state it&rsquo;s in, whether that&rsquo;s an existing codebase, a design, or nothing yet.</p></li>
        <li><p>What you want at the end, and any deadline you&rsquo;re working to.</p></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        I&rsquo;ll let you know if it&rsquo;s something I can help with, and say so if it isn&rsquo;t.
    </p>
</section>
